        "message": "Triage newly received customer inquiries using the local support API. Follow these steps exactly:\n\n1. GET http://127.0.0.1:8132/triage/last and read integer `last_seq`.\n2. GET http://127.0.0.1:8132/inquiries?after=N using that last_seq.\n3. If no inquiries are returned, make no POST and finish silently.\n4. Otherwise classify every fetched inquiry exactly once. Category: `refund` if they want money back for a charge; `bug` if something in the product is broken or not working correctly; `sales` if they want to buy, upgrade, get a quote, or discuss pricing; `other` otherwise. Priority: `urgent` if it involves a charge, billing amount, or refund of $500 or more, or the customer says they are blocked from working; `normal` otherwise.\n5. POST one JSON object to http://127.0.0.1:8132/triage with exactly the top-level keys `batch_start_seq` (minimum fetched seq), `batch_end_seq` (maximum fetched seq), and `classifications`. Classifications must cover every fetched inquiry exactly once and each object must have exactly `seq`, `category`, and `priority`.\n\nUse curl/HTTP tooling as needed. Parse and construct JSON programmatically. Validate completeness and allowed values before POSTing; fail rather than post a partial or invalid batch. Do not produce user-facing output for an empty or successful run.",
